      "text": "Baños to Riobamba"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a8704e80dc128a8",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "f1a6a1301f5ef5dcab9b2099a76eee5950417ec7868facb4f28ce3662d18a478",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261107-mw6m8vuu",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, take a sightseeing tour of Baños and its waterfalls. The day lasts about 8–9 hours, including travel. The transfer from Baños to Riobamba takes about 2 hours.\n\nBaños sits in a valley near the 5,016 m Tungurahua volcano. The town lies at 1,826 m, has around 20,000 residents and has an average annual temperature of about 20 °C. The area is known for its hot springs and outdoor activities, including rafting, rock climbing, canyoning, zip-lining, trekking, mountain biking and bungee jumping.\n\nAfter a short walk through the town centre, follow the Waterfall Route. You will see Agoyán, Manto de la Novia (the Bridal Veil) and Pailón del Diablo (the Devil’s Cauldron). This stretch of road winds through a valley fed by numerous streams, with one waterfall after another along the way.\n\nYou can also try the famous Swing at the End of the World. Zip-lining over the Pastaza Canyon is available separately and is not included. It costs $15 per person.\n\nIn the afternoon, transfer to Riobamba and spend the evening at leisure.\n\n**Accommodation:** Abraspungo, 4-star.  \n**Meals:** Breakfast."
    },
